  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Deathworld Veterans" id="0b0d-c34d-0b36-560d" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Veterans count woods or jungles as clear terrain. They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle terrain. If they do not move in the movement phase may see and shoot through 12&quot; of woods or jungle terrain instead of the normal 6&quot;. And they may infiltrate into woods or jungle in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Opps, Sorry Sir!" id="32a8-a559-293a-a999" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll a D6 for each Commissar before setting them up. On a roll of 1 the commissar has suffered an accident and cannot be used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ambush" id="1e9a-8f2f-238e-9e34" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Ambush set-up in Codex: Catachan page 20</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gung Ho" id="9d60-b109-f37e-cfa6" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests and can try to regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deathworld Toxins" id="1496-27c3-2f58-885c" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers may re-roll a failed roll to wound when using their rifles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Camouflage" id="2150-cbd0-329c-5f33" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers have a 3+ cover save in woods or jungle terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disappear" id="f24f-9916-55fe-8bf6" hidden="false">
      <description>Snipers never move. During your Movement phase, you may remove the sniper, representing the Sniper merging back into the shadows. Once removed, a Sniper may not return to the battlefield but doesn&apos;t count as having been killed for Victory point purposes. Snipers cannot claim table quarters or other objectives and don&apos;t have to be killed for an attacker to win Meat Grinder or Grand Assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Set-Up" id="e3ad-147a-43f5-a00a" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Booby Trap set-up in Codex: Catachan page 21</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ignore Cover Saves" id="ef50-ea59-9c80-ccd7" hidden="false">
      <description>Ignore cover saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Pinning" id="1644-75b3-7a1b-6398" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit that suffers one or more casualties from a booby trap must test for pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Plasma Charge" id="dc13-2a4b-c609-d6da" hidden="false">
      <description>The model that triggered the charge is hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shredder Mine" id="8879-cace-77eb-a230" hidden="false">
      <description>The mine is located D6&quot; away from the model that triggered it, in the direction indicated by the arrow on the Scatter dice. The player who laid the mine may place the flamer template with the narrow end at the location of the mine and positioned in such a manner that the model who triggered the trap is at least partially under the template. Any models touched by the template are hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Spring Mine" id="3d45-8e04-2e94-1f6d" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the large Ordnance Blast marker so that the central hole is over the model which triggered the trap. Then roll for scatter in the same way as you would for ordnance. Any models that are fully under the Ordnance Blast marker are hit automatically, and any that are partially under the Blast marker are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Trap" id="8e6a-cb86-d10e-8502" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the small Blast market so that the central hole is over the model that triggered the trap. Any models fully under the Blast marker are hit automatically and any partially under are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Placement" id="0f0f-2dd1-567e-7c66" hidden="false">
      <description>Each booby trap you take allows you to booby trap a 1&apos; square area.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jungle Fighters" id="5129-ecf7-d3f2-2a76" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll 3D6 and pick the highest to see how far the unit can move through jungle terrain. When pursuing and falling back through difficult terrain, they roll 3D6 and halve the result. They only become &apos;spooked&apos; on a roll of a triple one and only set off booby traps on any roll of a triple.
They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle.
They may infiltrate into woods or jungles in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Sly Marbo" id="a4d7-56cb-bf76-4ef6" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="model">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="135"/>
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Sly Marbo" id="afc7-977a-c1d4-a012" hidden="false" targetId="85b0-84d8-0f08-a2d7" type="profile"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Ripper Pistol" id="52e3-bb06-5689-86d7" hidden="false" typeId="b399-8a1b-bf0b-c5b7" typeName="Weapon">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="deb8-131d-bdcf-1376">12&apos;</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="24d8-2110-08fa-d844">X</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="25ce-028f-0aae-2855">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="d3f6-19e8-ac9e-ae13">Pistol</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Abilities" typeId="492d-1f80-b777-26f2">Re-roll failed rolls to wound</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="May Move" id="342c-70b4-c4bc-856f" hidden="false">
          <description>Unlike other Snipers, Sly may move after he has been revealed. You may removed him in your movement phase as if he was a normal Sniper, but write down new coordinates for a square adjacent to the one he disappeared from. He may reappear there using the Ambush rules from the start of his next turn.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Envenomed Blade" id="8f83-e0f0-15a9-df85" hidden="false">
          <description>Sly&apos;s knife is treated as a power weapon and the toxins on it allow Sly to re-roll any failed rolls to wound in close combat.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Always Operates Alone" id="2227-bae0-ca6b-4d86" hidden="false">
          <description>Sly is an independent character and may not join another unit.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Colonel Iron Hand Straken" id="eb4c-ad79-916c-8155" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="model">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="130"/>
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Straken" id="f069-948b-47a8-57f4" hidden="false" targetId="a095-74b7-64a2-04bc" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Shotgun" id="aa89-05a3-26db-24c7" hidden="false" targetId="9882-0cca-b1d2-8e0b" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Plasma Pistol" id="5421-665a-1439-b6d5" hidden="false" targetId="7b91-b670-d042-7c88" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Power Fist" id="dd8e-b6cf-7690-d0c6" hidden="false" targetId="a161-ed4b-bcb7-0a01" type="profile"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Unique Bionics" id="8ef6-6b2d-a5c7-ef83" hidden="false">
          <description>Straken&apos;s arm mimics the effect of a power fist, but devices in the chest allow him to strike using his initiative value instead of going last. In addition he counts as having bionics. If Straken ever makes his special bionics saving roll, then it is assumed his bionic arm has been disabled and he can no longer use it.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Gung Ho" id="19be-3ee9-f418-b3bc" hidden="false">
          <description>Straken, the unit he is with and any friendly units with a model within 6&quot; of him may re-roll failed Morale &amp; Pinning tests. In addition, they may always attempt to regroup.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
